--- Baseline route/page that must remain canonical ---

Backend route:  POST /api/v1/charge-planner/optimize
  - handler: internal/api/charge_planner_handler.go (*ChargePlannerHandler).Optimize
  - request: optimizeRequest { vehicle_id, target_soc, depart_by,
             rate_plan_id, max_amps, battery_capacity_kwh }
  - response: optimizeResponse { plan_id, schedule {start_time, end_time,
              duration_min, energy_kwh, estimated_cost}, savings_vs_now,
              hourly_rates [], surface }
  - persists: charge_plans row + chargePlanCreatedTotal counter
  - reads current SOC from stateReader (signal store)
  This is the canonical baseline. It MUST remain visible and clickable
  for users with ai_mode='off' and is NOT touched by this slice (except
  internal refactor extracting computeSchedule for code reuse — see
  charge_planner_handler.go diff; behaviour preserved by existing
  TestOptimize tests).

Frontend page:  web/src/features/charging/pages/SmartChargePage.tsx
  - rendered at path "smart-charge" by App.tsx
  - useSelectedVehicle() -> vehicleId, useRatePlans, useChargePlans,
    useOptimizeCharge, useApplySchedule hooks
  - GlassPanel sections: Settings form, "Charge Settings" form,
    optimized schedule result card, RateTimeline, Plans list
  - canonical Schedule button posts via useApplySchedule
  - No `if (aiEnabled) replace(...)` branches. The AI surface is added
    as a NEW <FadeIn>-wrapped panel ABOVE the form, conditionally
    rendered by withAiFeature('smart-charge-schedule-suggestion', …)
    so the baseline form stays canonical.

--- DTOs / shapes ---
api.optimizeRequest (from internal/api/charge_planner_handler.go):
  vehicle_id int64 (required); target_soc int (0-100); depart_by RFC3339;
  rate_plan_id string; max_amps int (default 32); battery_capacity_kwh
  float64 (default 75.0).

api.optimizeResponse:
  plan_id int64; schedule { start_time, end_time, duration_min,
  energy_kwh, estimated_cost }; savings_vs_now float64; hourly_rates
  [{ hour, rate, tier }]; surface "deterministic_charge_planner".

--- Existing hooks consumed by SmartChargePage ---
useSelectedVehicle, useRatePlans, useOptimizeCharge, useApplySchedule,
useChargePlans, useDateFormat, useFormatting — none touched.

