--- Off-mode invariant proof (per the prompt's focused off-mode block) ---

(a) POST /api/v1/ai/charging/schedule/draft returns 404 with body
    "not_found\n" when ai_mode='off'. Asserted by Go-side
    TestSmartChargeScheduleAIOffManualScheduleWorks subtests in
    internal/api/ai_smart_charge_schedule_handler_test.go. Status is
    asserted to be 404 (not 401/403/422 — which would risk leaking
    the existence of the route).
(b) POST /api/v1/charge-planner/optimize returns 200 with the
    canonical optimizeResponse envelope including a "surface" marker
    equal to "deterministic_charge_planner", proving the baseline
    handler ran end-to-end when ai_mode='off'. This is the "manual
    schedule works" semantic in the test name.
(c) Zero rendered elements with test ID
    "ai-feature-smart-charge-schedule-suggestion-root" when
    ai_mode='off'. Asserted by the Vitest test in
    web/src/features/charging/__tests__/
    TestSmartChargeScheduleAIOffManualScheduleWorks.test.tsx. The
    positive-control assertion (ai_mode='cloud' + toggle=true ->
    test ID present + data-ai-feature attr matches feature ID)
    proves the gate is not a permanent typo.

The React-side test exercises the corresponding UI invariant — the
AI section is absent in off mode AND present + correctly identified
in on mode. The Go-side test exercises the network invariant — the
AI route 404s in off mode AND the baseline route returns its
canonical envelope. Together they cover both halves of ADR-015 §I5
(hidden UI) and §I6 (404 routes) for this slice.

